# Merge behaviour for parallel work. See docs/development/parallel-work.md.

# Append-only files: git keeps BOTH sides instead of stopping the merge, which
# is what two streams appending a dated line each actually want.
#
# Correct ONLY where every change is an append and order does not matter.
# NEVER extend this to source files -- union-merging code produces something
# syntactically valid and semantically wrong, which is strictly worse than a
# conflict you can see.
devlog/journal.md   merge=union
CHANGELOG.md        merge=union

# Derived, not authored. package.json is the source of truth; on a conflict,
# take either side wholesale and run `npm install` to regenerate. Marking it
# -diff keeps it out of diffs and review noise, and is a standing reminder that
# hand-editing it is the wrong move: a hand-merged lockfile can look correct
# and install a different tree than either side intended.
package-lock.json   -diff linguist-generated=true

# Normalise line endings so a Windows contributor's checkout does not show
# every file as modified. Windows and macOS are supported day one via
# run-from-source (build-plan.md SSPlatform policy), so this is not theoretical.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
